  "body": "`scripts/release.ps1` phase 1 (preflight) now applies the same three checks `release.yml`'s publish job applies to `RELEASE_NOTES.md`: a `---` line exists, a non-empty section precedes it, and the first line names `-Version`. A cut with broken notes now fails before the version bump, instead of after the tag is pushed.\n\nWhy: the v0.14.0 cut replaced RELEASE_NOTES.md with its own section only. release.ps1 passed it, the tag went out, all five builds went green, and only the publish job failed (`RELEASE_NOTES.md has no '---' line`). The release had to be published by hand; the notes were repaired by #270.\n\nReadings (the new block run on its own):\n- main's notes, `-Version 0.14.0`: passes (\"0.14.0 section (83 lines) above the history\")\n- main's notes, `-Version 0.15.0`: refused, first section is 0.14.0\n- v0.14.0 tag's notes: refused, no `---` line\n- the whole script parses with 0 errors\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #272\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
